// waiver file for keymgr_dpe

`verilator_config

// Waive some width mismatch warnings in keymgr*.sv that come from addressing an
// array by literal elements of an enum that has extra entries. For example,
// keymgr_dpe_ops_e contains the 4 operations that reach the KMAC interface plus
// "OpDpeDisable" and "OpDpeLoadRootKey" entries, so its elements are represented
// by 3 bits. However, we use its literal values to index into things like the
// invalid_data array, which just has an entry for each of the 4 KMAC operations.
// Because $clog2(4) = 2, Verilator expects to address it with a 2-bit index and
// generates a warning.
lint_off -rule WIDTH -file "*/rtl/keymgr*.sv" -match "Bit extraction of var[*:0]*not * bits."
